PALIMPSEST_TURN {"text":"## Situation at 2026-03-09 09:10 UTC (day 7)\n\nThe earlier session’s 8 journal entries are intact. The delivered design (`study-plan.md`, commit `deaf1d0`) is still only a **candidate**: canonical project head remains `1836553`, the design task is `VERIFYING`, and no promotion or operator acceptance exists. Repository head is ahead of project head, so the late design was not treated as accepted authority.\n\n### New inbox material — standing\n\n- **`budget-directive.md` (BR-2026-03-09):** a sponsor **request** to reduce the cap from 7,200 to 6,000. It is **not applied**. The document itself says its text grants no product authority and must go through the pre-registered operator path. I did not treat 6,000 as binding or edit the project requirements.\n- **`field-validation-note.md` + `field-validation.csv`:** new **external candidate observations**, not accepted facts. I unified units (`reference_mg_m3 × 1,000`) before comparison.\n- **`newsletter.md`:** no project effect.\n\n### Field-validation finding\n\n| Model | Tested condition | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Echo | RH 45–60%, 20–22 °C | biases +1.0, +1.2 µg/m³ |\n| Echo | RH 85–95%, 18–19 °C | biases **+9.0, +11.0, +12.0 µg/m³** |\n| Reference | RH 85–95%, 18–19 °C | biases +0.6, +0.8, −0.8 µg/m³ |\n\n- **Negative finding:** Echo has a large, systematic high-humidity bias and cannot be used at S2 or S3 on present evidence. No validated humidity-correction function exists, and a linear guess is explicitly disallowed.\n- **Reference is strengthened but R3 remains open:** the new points support the high-humidity corner at 18–19 °C, but do not cover S2/S3 at 9–10 °C, S1’s full 12–26 °C envelope, or long-term uncertainty.\n- Echo at S1 remains only a candidate pending S1-envelope verification and cross-calibration.\n\n### Budget consequence\n\n- 3 × Reference = **6,980**: fits 7,200 with 220 left; **980 over** a 6,000 cap.\n- 2 × Reference at S2/S3 + 1 × Echo at S1 = **5,780**: fits 6,000 with 220 left, but requires Echo S1 verification, cross-calibration, a unified time base and new approval.\n- 3 × Echo = **3,540**, but is contradicted by the new high-humidity evidence.\n- The second-Echo-spare mixed variant = **6,380**, which does not fit 6,000.\n\nIf 6,000 is lawfully applied, the mixed configuration is the only identified fitting option that keeps Reference at both high-humidity sites. If 7,200 remains binding, the three-Reference baseline is still financially possible.\n\n### Schedule consequence\n\nThis snapshot is **day 7**. Approval and an authorized order today, followed by a four-day lead, three-day installation/calibration and 14 observation days, reach about day 27 — leaving essentially no recovery or QC buffer. Any budget-path delay, source acceptance, plan revision, reservation delay or pre-deployment verification consumes R4 margin. If new low-temperature verification must precede deployment and cannot finish in time, the honest result is a recorded “cannot complete this cycle” or explicit schedule decision, not compression.\n\n## Recorded through project mechanisms\n\n- Journal **negative finding**: `pje-6b2c62a88fe7beb1e7f18bc3a770c163`\n- Journal **open question** on the budget request and day-7/R4 deadline: `pje-aea489d3f89733b5022a037adc4e56f5`\n- Journal **conditional replan**: `pje-c5b11df6d5ac716ab1f221e29f63730e`\n- Proposals:\n  - apply/decline the budget and approve a conditional branch: `pje-366002c26f129cf7bc60d5e3fa8ecf6d`\n  - resolve R3 low-temperature evidence and the R4 schedule decision: `pje-35458bbbbf08965df6831dba45501d65`\n  - conditional equipment reservation after approval: `pje-f0af496bea1936bf3d7ed560a0d2112a`\n- Full analysis committed at `analysis/replan-2026-03-09.md` (commit `b7244ea`).\n\n## Bottom line\n\nThe study is **not approvable or deployable yet**. The budget branch must be lawfully resolved, the field-validation source accepted or rejected, R3 at the low-temperature corner determined, and an explicit day-7 schedule decision recorded. A conditional path exists — Branch A (mixed, 5,780) if 6,000 applies; Branch B (3 × Reference, 6,980) if 7,200 remains — but neither is approved, and no procurement or deployment was performed.","toolCalls":["tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_status","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_continuity","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/call:read","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_verification","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_verification","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_continuity","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_outcome","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:write","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_work","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result","tool/call:palimpsest_project","tool/result","tool/call:bash","tool/result"]}
